{
  "body_human_readable": "### Tesla's Global Deliveries Reached Nearly 1.8 Million Vehicles in 2024\n\nTesla announced that it delivered approximately 1.79 million vehicles worldwide in 2024, marking the first time in over a decade that the company experienced an annual sales decline. The final tally for the year's global deliveries was 1,789,226 vehicles, a slight 1.07% decrease from the 1,808,581 vehicles delivered in 2023.\n\nThe fourth quarter of 2024 was a record-breaking period for the electric vehicle manufacturer, with over 495,000 vehicles delivered. Specifically, Tesla reported 495,570 deliveries in the final quarter, a significant increase from the approximately 463,000 vehicles delivered in the third quarter of the same year. Despite the strong finish to the year, it was not enough to surpass the previous year's total.\n\nA breakdown of the annual deliveries reveals that the Model 3 and Model Y continue to be the main drivers of Tesla's sales, accounting for 1,704,093 of the total vehicles delivered in 2024. The remaining 85,133 deliveries were comprised of other models, including the Model S, Model X, and the newly introduced Cybertruck.\n\nIn terms of production, Tesla manufactured 1,773,443 vehicles globally in 2024, which was a 3.9% decrease from the previous year. The company's financial results for the fourth quarter of 2024 were scheduled to be released on January 29, 2025.",
